qtgrass (0.5.1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix IAU PROJ_INFO completeness: after g.proj creates a location from an
    IAU_2015 (or any spherical body) SRID, fixupProjInfo() queries the PROJ 9
    C API (proj_get_ellipsoid / proj_ellipsoid_get_parameters) for the
    authoritative semi-major axis and eccentricity², then rewrites PROJ_INFO
    with the required "a:" and "es:" keys that GRASS's G_gisinit() needs.
    Without these GRASS emits "No ellipsoid info given in file" and crashes.
  * Auto-repair existing locations: openMapset() now calls repairProjInfo()
    on the location's PERMANENT directory every time a mapset is opened.
    It reads PROJ_SRID (or falls back to PROJ_WKT) to reconstruct the
    correct ellipsoid parameters via PROJ, then patches PROJ_INFO in-place.
    Pre-existing broken locations (e.g. MarsMercator) are fixed transparently
    on the first open after this update.
  * Planetary menu scan deferred until session is open: scanAvailableModules()
    now takes a QProcessEnvironment (from buildSubprocessEnv) so modules run
    with a valid GISRC; scan runs by full path; GrassApp rebuilds the menu on
    GrassEnv::mapsetChanged so it is populated after a session is selected.

